From d73692dd91341d4303b779bc27076940f67b8bb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joe Finzel <joe@sudmix.de>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:46:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau/gsp: keep MOT on address-only AUX transfers

r535_dp_aux_xfer() clears I2C_MOT on every address-only request. The
DRM I2C-over-AUX helper begins each I2C message with an address-only
request that has MOT set, so on GSP-RM the start of every message
becomes a stop condition on the DDC bus.

E-DDC resets the segment pointer (I2C address 0x30) on a stop. The
segment write is thus lost before the following read at 0x50, and the
sink returns segment 0 again: EDID blocks 2 and 3 read back as blocks 0
and 1. On a Dell AW2723DF connected to an RTX 3070 Ti, block 2 is its
DisplayID extension with the only 2560x1440@240Hz timing; the kernel
saw a second copy of the base block instead, and the highest mode
offered was 2560x1440@144Hz. Windows reads the correct block from the
same monitor.

Keep the MOT bit the caller requested. The final address-only request
that closes a transfer has MOT cleared by the helper already, so stops
are unchanged. The non-GSP AUX path (nvkm_i2c_aux_xfer) passes the
request type through as well.

Fixes: 9e9944449023 ("drm/nouveau/disp/r535: initial support")
Signed-off-by: Joe Finzel <joe@sudmix.de>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/disp.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/disp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/disp.c
index f5f22173fc2..729e0d5cd42 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/disp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/disp.c
@@ -1081,10 +1081,13 @@ r535_dp_aux_xfer(struct nvkm_outp *outp, u8 type, u32 addr, u8 *data, u8 *psize)
 		ctrl->displayId = BIT(outp->index);
 		ctrl->bAddrOnly = !size;
 		ctrl->cmd = type;
-		if (ctrl->bAddrOnly) {
+		/*
+		 * Keep the caller's MOT bit: the DRM I2C-over-AUX helper starts each
+		 * message with an address-only request with MOT set, and clearing it
+		 * turns that start into a stop.
+		 */
+		if (ctrl->bAddrOnly)
 			ctrl->cmd = NVDEF_SET(ctrl->cmd, NV0073_CTRL, DP_AUXCH_CMD, REQ_TYPE, WRITE);
-			ctrl->cmd = NVDEF_SET(ctrl->cmd, NV0073_CTRL, DP_AUXCH_CMD,  I2C_MOT, FALSE);
-		}
 		ctrl->addr = addr;
 		ctrl->size = !ctrl->bAddrOnly ? (size - 1) : 0;
 		memcpy(ctrl->data, data, size);
-- 
